{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I will be that I will be.</b> And afterward He said, ״כֹּה תֹאמַר אֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַנִי אֲלֵיכֶם״ — and further, what is the meaning of what it says, ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל מֹשֶׁה אֶהְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה״? It should have said, ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֵלָיו״, since it is with Moses that He is speaking. And it appears that the expression ״אֶהְיֶה״ signifies that the Holy One, blessed be He, will be with them, and Moses was afraid of two kinds of fear: the first, that he himself would be harmed by this mission; the second, that the Egyptians would not let them go. But Israel feared only that Pharaoh would not let them go. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses, ״אֶהְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה״, in the same manner that He said to him above (Exodus 3:12), ״כִּי אֶהְיֶה עִמָּךָ״ — including all of Israel as well, that the Egyptians would not harm them and would let them go out. But to Israel you shall say, ״אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַנִי אֲלֵיכֶם״, for there is no need to inform them that ״I will be with you״ in this mission, but Moses needed both." "And there are those who say that the statement ״אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה״ is the giving of a reason for the name ״אֶהְיֶה״, for this is why I am called by the name ״אֶהְיֶה״ — because I am and I will be in all times, in the past, in the present, and in the future. Therefore He said, ״כֹּה תֹאמַר אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַנִי״, for Israel do not need all that, that is, the giving of a reason. And what He said further, ״כֹּה תֹאמַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֱלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵיכֶם״ etc. — for it is not fitting that He be mentioned by this essential name, but only by the name ״אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם״ etc. This is what it says (Exodus 3:15), ״זֶה שְּׁמִי לְעֹלָם״ — that is, ״אֶהְיֶה״; ״וְזֶה זִכְרִי לְדֹר דֹּר״ — this is the name ״אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם״, by which He will always be mentioned, not by the essential name." "And it appears to me to explain, that since the name אֶהְיֶה is derived from the root הֲוָיָה and signifies His eternity — for He, blessed be He, was and will be — therefore He said, ״זֶה שְּׁמִי לְעֹלָם״ (Exodus 3:15), meaning: this, my name, signifies that I am לְעוֹלָם, meaning from eternity to eternity my existence is the same. And ״זֶה זִכְרִי לְדֹר דֹּר״ (Exodus 3:15) — this is what I said, that I am called ״אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב״ (Exodus 3:15), to be mentioned by this name always, signifying that not only is my existence equal from my own side in all times, but furthermore, in all times my name will be mentioned upon those who fear HaShem and think upon His name, in each and every generation, equally the same — when the children hold fast to the deeds of their holy fathers, in the manner that I did for Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, when I was called by my name upon each and every one individually, so too in each and every generation my name will be mentioned upon all the survivors whom HaShem calls (Joel 3:5). This is what is stated: ״וְזֶה זִכְרִי לְדֹר דֹּר״." "And according to the prophecy of Ezekiel, from which it is implied that Israel were in Egypt wicked and sinful — if so, there was no merit in their hand at all, and they were redeemed only by the merit of two things: (1) for the sake of His great name, which is with them in exile, as it were, as He senses their distress, as it is written (Exodus 3:19) ״כִּי יָדַעְתִּי אֶת מַכְאוֹבָיו״, and as it is written (Joshua 7:9) ״וּמַה תַּעֲשֵׂה לְשִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל״; (2) in the merit of the fathers. Therefore He said, ״כֹּה תֹאמַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַנִי אֲלֵיכֶם״ (Exodus 3:14) — He employed specifically this name, which signifies ״עִמּוֹ אָנֹכִי בְצָרָה״ (Psalms 91:15). ״וַיֹּאמֶר עוֹד כֹּה תֹאמַר וְגוֹ׳ ה׳ אֱלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵיכֶם״ etc. (Exodus 3:15) — that is, the merit of the fathers. These two combined to bring them out from distress to relief."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:25.203376404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}